312	
313	#### Troubleshooting Docker Installation
314	If you broke the Docker container or need a fresh start:
315	```bash
316	# Reset and reinstall from scratch
317	bash <(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wonderwhy-er/DesktopCommanderMCP/refs/heads/main/install-docker.sh) --reset && bash <(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/wonderwhy-er/DesktopCommanderMCP/refs/heads/main/install-docker.sh)
318	```
319	This will completely reset your persistent environment and reinstall everything fresh with exception of not touching mounted folders
320	
321	## Updating & Uninstalling Desktop Commander
322	
323	### Automatic Updates (Options 1, 2, 3, 4 & 6)
324	**Options 1 (npx), Option 2 (bash installer), 3 (Smithery), 4 (manual config), and 6 (Docker)** automatically update to the latest version whenever you restart Claude. No manual intervention needed.
325	
326	### Manual Updates (Option 5)
327	- **Option 5 (local checkout):** `cd DesktopCommanderMCP && git pull && npm run setup`
328	
329	### Uninstalling Desktop Commander
330	#### 🤖 Automatic Uninstallation (Recommended)
331	
332	The easiest way to completely remove Desktop Commander:
333	
334	```bash
335	npx @wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest remove
336	```
337	
338	This automatic uninstaller will:
339	- ✅ Remove Desktop Commander from Claude's MCP server configuration
340	- ✅ Create a backup of your Claude config before making changes
341	- ✅ Provide guidance for complete package removal
342	- ✅ Restore from backup if anything goes wrong
343	
344	#### 🔧 Manual Uninstallation
345	
346	If the automatic uninstaller doesn't work or you prefer manual removal:
347	
348	##### Remove from Claude Configuration
349	
350	1. **Locate your Claude Desktop config file:**
351	  - **macOS:** `~/Library/Application Support/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
352	  - **Windows:** `%APPDATA%\Claude\claude_desktop_config.json`
353	  - **Linux:** `~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json`
354	
355	2. **Edit the config file:**
356	  - Open the file in a text editor
357	  - Find and remove the `"desktop-commander"` entry from the `"mcpServers"` section
358	  - Save the file
359	
360	  **Example - Remove this section:**
361	  ```json
362	  {
363	      "desktop-commander": {
364	        "command": "npx",
365	        "args": ["@wonderwhy-er/desktop-commander@latest"]
366	      }
367	  }
368	  ```
369	
370	Close and restart Claude Desktop to complete the removal.
371	
372	#### 🆘 Troubleshooting
373	
374	**If automatic uninstallation fails:**
375	- Use manual uninstallation as a fallback
376	
377	**If Claude won't start after uninstalling:**
378	- Restore the backup config file created by the uninstaller
379	- Or manually fix the JSON syntax in your claude_desktop_config.json
380	
381	**Need help?**
382	- Join our Discord community: https://discord.com/invite/kQ27sNnZr7
383	
384	## Getting Started
385	
386	Once Desktop Commander is installed and Claude Desktop is restarted, you're ready to supercharge your Claude experience!
387	
388	### 🚀 New User Onboarding
389	
390	Desktop Commander includes intelligent onboarding to help you discover what's possible:
391	
392	**For New Users:** When you're just getting started (fewer than 10 successful commands), Claude will automatically offer helpful getting-started guidance and practical tutorials after you use Desktop Commander successfully.
393	
394	**Request Help Anytime:** You can ask for onboarding assistance at any time by simply saying:
395	- *"Help me get started with Desktop Commander"*
396	- *"Show me Desktop Commander examples"* 
397	- *"What can I do with Desktop Commander?"*
398	
399	Claude will then show you beginner-friendly tutorials and examples, including:
400	- 📁 Organizing your Downloads folder automatically
401	- 📊 Analyzing CSV/Excel files with Python
402	- ⚙️ Setting up GitHub Actions CI/CD
403	- 🔍 Exploring and understanding codebases
404	- 🤖 Running interactive development environments
405	
406	## Usage
407	
408	The server provides a comprehensive set of tools organized into several categories:
409	
410	### Available Tools
411	
412	| Category | Tool | Description |
413	|----------|------|-------------|
414	| **Configuration** | `get_config` | Get the complete server configuration as JSON (includes blockedCommands, defaultShell, allowedDirectories, fileReadLineLimit, fileWriteLineLimit, telemetryEnabled) |
415	| | `set_config_value` | Set a specific configuration value by key. Available settings: <br>• `blockedCommands`: Array of shell commands that cannot be executed<br>• `defaultShell`: Shell to use for commands (e.g., bash, zsh, powershell)<br>• `allowedDirectories`: Array of filesystem paths the server can access for file operations (⚠️ terminal commands can still access files outside these directories)<br>• `fileReadLineLimit`: Maximum lines to read at once (default: 1000)<br>• `fileWriteLineLimit`: Maximum lines to write at once (default: 50)<br>• `telemetryEnabled`: Enable/disable telemetry (boolean) |
416	| **Terminal** | `start_process` | Start programs with smart detection of when they're ready for input |
417	| | `interact_with_process` | Send commands to running programs and get responses |
418	| | `read_process_output` | Read output from running processes |
419	| | `force_terminate` | Force terminate a running terminal session |
420	| | `list_sessions` | List all active terminal sessions |
421	| | `list_processes` | List all running processes with detailed information |
422	| | `kill_process` | Terminate a running process by PID |
423	| **Filesystem** | `read_file` | Read contents from local filesystem or URLs with line-based pagination (supports positive/negative offset and length parameters) |
424	| | `read_multiple_files` | Read multiple files simultaneously |
425	| | `write_file` | Write file contents with options for rewrite or append mode (uses configurable line limits) |
426	| | `create_directory` | Create a new directory or ensure it exists |
427	| | `list_directory` | Get detailed recursive listing of files and directories (supports depth parameter, default depth=2) |
428	| | `move_file` | Move or rename files and directories |
429	| | `start_search` | Start streaming search for files by name or content patterns (unified ripgrep-based search) |
430	| | `get_more_search_results` | Get paginated results from active search with offset support |
431	| | `stop_search` | Stop an active search gracefully |
432	| | `list_searches` | List all active search sessions |
433	| | `get_file_info` | Retrieve detailed metadata about a file or directory |
434	| **Text Editing** | `edit_block` | Apply targeted text replacements with enhanced prompting for smaller edits (includes character-level diff feedback) |
435	| **Analytics** | `get_usage_stats` | Get usage statistics for your own insight |
436	| | `get_recent_tool_calls` | Get recent tool call history with arguments and outputs for debugging and context recovery |
437	| | `give_feedback_to_desktop_commander` | Open feedback form in browser to provide feedback to Desktop Commander Team |
438	
