52	
53	### Component Details
54	
55	1. **Input Layer**
56	   - `spark_code_input.py`: Source PySpark code for optimization
57	   - `run_client.py`: Client startup and configuration
58	
59	2. **MCP Client Layer**
60	   - Tools Interface: Protocol-compliant tool invocation
61	
62	3. **MCP Server Layer**
63	   - `run_server.py`: Server initialization
64	   - Tool Registry: Optimization and analysis tools
65	   - Protocol Handler: MCP request/response management
66	
67	4. **Resource Layer**
68	   - Claude AI: Code analysis and optimization
69	   - PySpark Runtime: Code execution and validation
70	
71	5. **Output Layer**
72	   - `optimized_spark_code.py`: Optimized code
73	   - `performance_analysis.md`: Detailed analysis
74	
75	This workflow illustrates:
76	1. Input PySpark code submission
77	2. MCP protocol handling and routing
78	3. Claude AI analysis and optimization
79	4. Code transformation and validation
80	5. Performance analysis and reporting
81	
82	## Architecture
83	
84	This project follows the Model Context Protocol architecture for standardized AI model interactions:
85	
86	```
87	┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐      ┌──────────────────┐
88	│                  │      │   MCP Server     │      │    Resources     │
89	│   MCP Client     │      │  (SparkMCPServer)│      │                  │
90	│ (SparkMCPClient) │      │                  │      │ ┌──────────────┐ │
91	│                  │      │    ┌─────────┐   │      │ │  Claude AI   │ │
92	│   ┌─────────┐    │      │    │ Tools   │   │ <──> │ │   Model      │ │
93	│   │ Tools   │    │      │    │Registry │   │      │ └──────────────┘ │
94	│   │Interface│    │ <──> │    └─────────┘   │      │                  │
95	│   └─────────┘    │      │    ┌─────────┐   │      │ ┌──────────────┐ │
96	│                  │      │    │Protocol │   │      │ │  PySpark     │ │
97	│                  │      │    │Handler  │   │      │ │  Runtime     │ │
98	│                  │      │    └─────────┘   │      │ └──────────────┘ │
99	└──────────────────┘      └──────────────────┘      └──────────────────┘
100	
101	        │                         │                          │
102	        │                         │                          │
103	        v                         v                          v
104	┌──────────────┐          ┌──────────────┐           ┌──────────────┐
105	│  Available   │          │  Registered  │           │   External   │
106	│    Tools     │          │    Tools     │           │  Resources   │
107	├──────────────┤          ├──────────────┤           ├──────────────┤
108	│optimize_code │          │optimize_code │           │ Claude API   │
109	│analyze_perf  │          │analyze_perf  │           │ Spark Engine │
110	└──────────────┘          └──────────────┘           └──────────────┘
111	```
112	
113	### Components
114	
115	1. **MCP Client**
116	   - Provides tool interface for code optimization
117	   - Handles async communication with server
118	   - Manages file I/O for code generation
119	
120	2. **MCP Server**
121	   - Implements MCP protocol handlers
122	   - Manages tool registry and execution
123	   - Coordinates between client and resources
124	
125	3. **Resources**
126	   - Claude AI: Provides code optimization intelligence
127	   - PySpark Runtime: Executes and validates optimizations
128	
129	### Protocol Flow
130	
131	1. Client sends optimization request via MCP protocol
132	2. Server validates request and invokes appropriate tool
133	3. Tool utilizes Claude AI for optimization
134	4. Optimized code is returned via MCP response
135	5. Client saves and validates the optimized code
136	
137	### End-to-End Functionality
138	
139	```mermaid
140	sequenceDiagram
141	    participant U as User
142	    participant C as MCP Client
143	    participant S as MCP Server
144	    participant AI as Claude AI
145	    participant P as PySpark Runtime
146	
147	    U->>C: Submit Spark Code
148	    C->>S: Send Optimization Request
149	    S->>AI: Analyze Code
150	    AI-->>S: Optimization Suggestions
151	    S->>C: Return Optimized Code
152	    C->>P: Run Original Code
153	    C->>P: Run Optimized Code
154	    P-->>C: Execution Results
155	    C->>C: Generate Analysis
156	    C-->>U: Final Report
157	```
158	
159	1. **Code Submission**
160	   - User places PySpark code in `v1/input/spark_code_input.py`
161	   - Code is read by the MCP client
162	
163	2. **Optimization Process**
164	   - MCP client connects to server via standardized protocol
165	   - Server forwards code to Claude AI for analysis
166	   - AI suggests optimizations based on best practices
167	   - Server validates and processes suggestions
168	
169	3. **Code Generation**
170	   - Optimized code saved to `v1/output/optimized_spark_code.py`
171	   - Includes detailed comments explaining optimizations
172	   - Maintains original code structure while improving performance
173	
174	4. **Performance Analysis**
175	   - Both versions executed in PySpark runtime
176	   - Execution times compared
177	   - Results validated for correctness
178	   - Metrics collected and analyzed
179	
180	5. **Results Generation**
181	   - Comprehensive analysis in `v1/output/performance_analysis.md`
182	   - Side-by-side execution comparison
183	   - Performance improvement statistics
184	   - Optimization explanations and rationale
185	
